KG42.register("clusters-0df91787ed59045eca63d957",{"id":"04-energy_collectives::v142-d-K001","paper":"04-energy_collectives","label":"Optimal community clearing and internal price coordination","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Optimal community clearing and internal price coordination","market_meaning":"Given member asset feasibility, cost preferences, and the collective agreement, the community manager coordinates exchange quantities and the collective objective; the prices corresponding to internal balance enter member decisions. Centralized optimization, ADMM implementation, and perfectly competitive equilibrium retain their respective conditions, and the current candidate cannot yet confirm the complete mathematical linkage among the three.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The chains belong to the same community mechanism. Information disclosure for centralized optimization, the ADMM supervisory node, perfectly competitive equilibrium, and 24-hour clearing in the case with fixed daily electricity consumption each have their respective applicability; unresolved discrepancies remain in the appendix's export signs and g parameters, so conditional correspondence cannot be elevated to confirmed equivalence.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The objective, feasible region, manager interface, and internal prices jointly explain how a community allocation decision is formed and coordinated, with complementary decision dependencies. Trading participation rights and specific settlement arrangements have separate boundaries; this cluster does not use the shared manager node as the basis for merging.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Covers the clearing feasible region, supervision conditions, and the specified intraday clearing scope."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Adds the collective objective, the overall convexity premise, and the conditional correspondence between centralized optimization and equilibrium."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Specifies the manager's responsibilities for the common agreement and external exchanges; the unresolved formulation in its equilibrium objective is retained as written."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Explains how internal prices enter members' individual decisions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Adds the dual relationship between internal prices and the balance in centralized clearing."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-C01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E32"],"rationale":"The collective objective and feasibility conditions of the same exchange problem are complementary; the local constraints in the extended costs do not thereby become additional independent market rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-C02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::theta::theta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E11"],"rationale":"The common agreement enters the collective objective through the manager model; this mapping does not confirm that Eq. (19) and that objective have the same parameter list."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-C03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"Links only the internal exchange balance shared by the two formulations with its price interpretation; this does not establish that all balance equations in the appendix are consistent with Eq. (1)."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-C04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_c","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"The internal balance multiplier in the centralized model and the internal trading price in perfectly competitive equilibrium correspond to one another and enter member objectives; the mapping is limited to this price interface."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-C05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E19","v141-b-g03-E20"],"rationale":"The source describes centralized optimization and individual price responses as corresponding representations under different conditions. This candidate correspondence is recorded here, with mathematical discrepancies listed separately as gaps, without counting them as two independent clearing rules."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E31"],"rationale":"Node references to the same M01 community manager in the objective, agreement interface, and supervision; only display is unified, while responsibilities and implementation conditions are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E14"],"rationale":"Allocation and price perspectives on the same community-clearing function; their complete formulas are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"Both occurrences refer to the function of internal community trading prices, rather than members' perceived prices."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R002::x::p_j"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"Members' net production quantities in the same exchange problem, retaining their local roles in the feasible region and objective separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X002","v141-c-R002::x::q_j","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-q_j"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"The definition and internal balance jointly support the correspondence between quantities exchanged by members with the community; their roles in feasibility, the collective objective, and individual price responses are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X003","v141-c-R002::x::alpha_j"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10"],"rationale":"All are members' external import quantities in Eq. (1), retaining the declaration and constraint roles in each chain."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X004","v141-c-R002::x::beta_j"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10"],"rationale":"All are members' external export quantities in Eq. (1); this identity mapping does not correct the export signs in the appendix."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X005","v141-c-R002::x::q_imp","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-qimp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same total community import quantity appears throughout the aggregate balance, collective objective, and manager interface; this does not remove the uncertainty about the optimization domain in Eq. (19)."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X006","v141-c-R002::x::q_exp","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-qexp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The definitions of total export quantity are consistent, but the concern that Eq. (19a) does not correctly distinguish the two parameters is retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-P001","v141-c-R002::theta::n"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"The same number of collective members, used respectively to index the clearing constraints and the summation in the objective."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M11","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"The two procedural constraints express the same requirement that all members disclose their utility curves during centralized optimization; only display is unified, and the requirement is not extended to decomposition algorithms."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The signs of β_j differ between Eq. (1b) and appendix Eqs. (16b) and (18b); the export price term in (18a) is also not directly consistent with the corresponding sign in (21d). The equivalence assertion in R002-C006 must be retained as a source claim and cannot serve as a connection for which mathematical verification has been completed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E19","v141-b-g03-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the export direction, objective signs, and KKT derivation equation by equation, with upstream clarification of whether these are transcription issues or discrepancies in the original text; do not correct the frozen expressions in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Eq. (19a), retained in R003-C003, uses q_imp repeatedly, unlike the interface parameter table for Eq. (1); whether Γ includes manager variables is unclear, and the connection between the independent manager objective and the market multiplier conditions has also not been fully established.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the parameters and decision domain of Eq. (19), and explain how its prices or coupling constraints enter the equilibrium conditions; do not merge the two objective expressions before this is done."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The asset variables, extended costs, and feasible set of R002 have not yet formed a complete executable specification; theta accommodates both parameters and additional variables. A guarantee of global optimality also requires overall convexity and cannot be inferred from the convexity of asset costs alone.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R002::x::u_ij","v141-c-R002::theta::theta","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have C specify the linkage between assets and net production, the feasible set, the scope of optimization variables, and the units, and check the conditions under which h, g, and the feasible region satisfy overall convexity."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G04","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The 24-hour constraints and ADMM supervision are procedural descriptions in the frozen chain; complete temporal coupling, iteration conditions, and stopping conditions have not yet been incorporated. R004-C002 is labeled (21b), but its direct citations primarily point to (17) and (18), and π_j has not been established as an object in this chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E16","v141-b-g03-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If this is extended into an executable workflow, have C supplement the corresponding constraints and objects; verify and correct the evidence binding for (21b), define the multipliers used, and continue to retain the temporal scope of the case."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G05","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The manager entity and its interface objective g continue to be jointly represented by the existing node; v141-b-g01-P01 has not yet been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P01"],"required_work":"Manually assess whether the entity and the objective function need separate representations; currently retain only the proposal reference and do not add nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G06","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence cited by this cluster retains unverified status. Assembly proceeds on the basis of eligibility as an experimental candidate and has not undergone independent source or scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, manually check the original passages used and their mathematical transcription, especially the sign discrepancies above; do not treat candidate usability as source correctness."}]},"rule_refs":["04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R001","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R002","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R003","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R004","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-79bf800032a75283","COMP-f0015e75a5829a38","KG31-3fa7c9f6716d2240","KG31-589dd70d32471060","KG31-66660a21725d3de3"]});
